{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42472 - PROTEIN:5782",
  "verbalization": "N-Methyltyramine is implicated in the target pathway leading to DMS-273 through a series of enzymatic interactions. The evidence suggests that N-Methyltyramine acts as a target for Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol. These compounds are all linked to DMS-273, indicating a potential mechanism where N-Methyltyramine indirectly influences DMS-273 through the SDR family. The recurring involvement of the SDR family and the shared target of DMS-273 suggests a possible role in metabolic or signaling pathways, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a pathway where N-Methyltyramine may modulate the activity of SDR family members, which in turn affect DMS-273, though the precise molecular interactions require further investigation.",
